Drop image files into this folder using these EXACT names.
The site checks for them automatically — no code editing needed.
Any slot without a matching file just keeps its placeholder, so you
can add these gradually, in any order.

  first-photo.jpg        Origin section polaroid
  project.jpg             The Lore — project arc
  fest.jpg                 The Lore — college fest
  garba.jpg                The Lore — Garba night (used only if garba.mp4 is missing)
  late-night-call.jpg      The Lore — 2:13 AM archive
  wall-1.jpg  wall-2.jpg  wall-3.jpg  wall-4.jpg  wall-5.jpg  wall-6.jpg
                            Archive collage, six cards. Each is used only
                            if the matching wall-N.mp4 in assets/videos
                            isn't present — video always wins over photo
                            for the same number.
  favorite.jpg              Truth section — your favorite photo together

Any common image format works (.jpg, .jpeg, .png, .webp) — just
update the matching data-photo="assets/photos/..." path in index.html
if you use a different extension than .jpg.

Keep files reasonably compressed (under ~500KB each) so the site
loads fast — most phone photos are much larger than that by default.
